      <!-- SECTION 4: SEO prose -->
      <section class="neutral-bg">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="prose">
            <h2>About Dragon Professional 16 licensing in Australia</h2>
            <p>Dragon Professional 16 is sold in Australia through Voice Recognition Australia (VRA), which has been the authorised Dragon reseller in Australia for over 25 years. Unlike buying through international stores, purchasing through VRA gives you local support, Australian pricing in AUD, and access to VRA's deployment and onboarding team.</p>
            <p>The key choice most Australian buyers face is between the perpetual licence ($994), the upgrade ($495 for existing v15 owners), and the annual subscription ($595/yr). For most individuals, the perpetual licence is the most cost-effective long-term option. The subscription makes sense when you need the software on multiple PCs or prefer annual billing cycles.</p>
            <h2>Dragon vs Windows built-in voice tools</h2>
            <p>Microsoft Windows 11 includes two built-in voice tools: Voice Typing (Win+H shortcut) and Voice Access. Both require an internet connection to function, per Microsoft's own documentation. Dragon Professional 16, once installed and activated, operates without an internet connection.</p>
            <p>The practical difference matters most for professionals who work with sensitive documents, operate in environments with limited connectivity, or need consistent accuracy in specialised vocabulary. Windows Voice Typing is a reasonable option for light, occasional dictation in a connected environment. It is not designed for the sustained, high-accuracy, customised dictation workflows that Dragon Professional 16 is built for.</p>
            <h2>What Dragon Professional 16 does not do</h2>
            <p>It is worth being clear about the boundaries of Dragon Professional 16, based on official Nuance support documentation. The software is designed for single-speaker dictation and transcription. It will not reliably transcribe multi-speaker conversations, meetings, or interviews. If you need meeting transcription, Dragon Professional 16 is not the right tool.</p>
            <p>Dragon Professional 16 is also a Windows-only product. Nuance discontinued Dragon for Mac. There is no v16 Mac version. If you need cross-platform dictation that includes Mac, look at cloud-based alternatives.</p>
            <h2>System requirements</h2>
            <p>Dragon Professional 16 requires Windows 10 or Windows 11 (32-bit or 64-bit). The official data sheet cites 8GB free disk space; the release notes and enterprise installation guide reference 12GB - allow at least 12GB to be safe. An internet connection is required for the initial download and activation, but not for ongoing use.</p>
            <p>Supported audio input formats for transcription include MP3, WAV, WMA, DS2, and DSS. Apple AirPods are not supported for live dictation. A dedicated USB dictation microphone or headset is recommended for best accuracy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
